  "surprise": "Keep: 548 (535, 562, 546) against 701's 531 (510, 529, 553), up on two seeds (701's mean read from its pod logs; its results were not yet in results/ when this was recorded). The mechanism prediction held, and more: at 0 thoughts this model solves 329 (347, 319, 321) against 701's 479 (466, 476, 496), so the 8-vs-0 gap is 219 theorems here against 52 for 701; per-sample eval accuracy at 0 thoughts is 7-9% against 701's 20-23%, while at 8 thoughts both are 30-31%. I was wrong about 701: its gap did not close to within noise, so the mixed-count fine-tune weakens the thoughts rather than erasing them. Sampling every target 32 times at 8 thoughts found about as many RL targets as 701's 8 at each of 0/2/4/8 (956 against 942 after three rounds) in the same three rounds (469-549 s each, 1,460-1,548 s charged). Same-seed pretrained models vary more than expected: seed 0 started at 4.5% sample accuracy at 8 thoughts against 701's 9.6%, and still ended at 535 against 510.",
